- op: create  # d6f8
  at: '2026-08-04T07:38:33Z'  # d6f8
  by: agent  # d6f8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d6f8
  clock: 1  # d6f8
  nonce: d6f8  # d6f8
  data:  # d6f8
    kind: invariant  # d6f8
    title: "A definition the DDG never recorded yields False (accounted-for) instead of None (unknown) — unmodelled constructs read as confident negatives"  # d6f8
    status: violated  # d6f8
    priority: 0  # d6f8
    parent:  # d6f8
    tags:  # d6f8
    - taint  # d6f8
    - adr_0017  # d6f8
    - dataflow  # d6f8
    isbefore: []  # d6f8
    duplicate_of: []  # d6f8
    not_duplicate_of: []  # d6f8
    pr_ref:  # d6f8
    description: "VERIFIED LIVE DEFECT. Found by a review panel, reproduced independently:\n\n  _ddg_taint_reaches(\"f\", [1], [9], {})  ->  False\n\nFalse is the walk's \"ran to completion and ACCOUNTED FOR THE VALUE AT EVERY\nSTEP\" verdict -- the only value that could ever license removing a reported\nflow. Here the DDG contains nothing at all about line 1. Nothing was accounted\nfor. The walk cannot distinguish \"this definition provably goes nowhere\" from\n\"the extractor never recorded this definition\".\n\nMECHANISM. The walk does `uses = ddg_uses.get((symbol_id, line))` and, when\nempty, `continue`s WITHOUT setting `escaped`. Every other way of losing the\nvalue sets it; this one does not.\n\nWHY IT IS NOT HYPOTHETICAL -- THE GAP IS SELF-DOCUMENTED. cfg_nodes/go.yaml\nsays, in the file itself:\n  \"Known gap, disclosed: the `initializer` of an if_statement\n   (`if err := do(); err != nil`) and of a for_clause is not reached by the\n   conditional/loop hooks... Those bindings are therefore still invisible to\n   def/use.\"\nThe panel counted 700 of 6,596 `if` statements in caddy carrying a call in the\ninitializer. So there is a large, known, per-language population of constructs\nthe def/use extractor does not see -- and the walk converts every one of them\ninto a confident negative instead of an unknown.\n\nTHE PANEL REPRODUCED THE CADDY INCIDENT FLOW THROUGH THIS PATH.\n  cwd, _ := os.Getwd()\n  msg := \"cwd=\" + cwd\n  if n, err := fmt.Printf(\"%s\", msg); ...\nyields exactly one DDG edge, (cwd, 3, 4). msg's use at line 5 does not exist in\nthe DDG. The walk pops line 4, finds no uses, continues, records NO escape, and\nreturns False. That is a REAL leak -- one of the three verified-real removals\nfrom the 2026-08-03 arm -- refuted with no escape flagged anywhere.\n\nRELATIONSHIP TO THE OTHER OPEN ITEMS. INV-busis frames the blocker as non-call\nescape sites needing field-sensitivity. This is a THIRD fact that framing\nmissed: not \"journey ended\", not \"went somewhere unfollowable\", but \"the use\nwas never recorded because the construct is not modelled\". Unlike the other\ntwo it is INVISIBLE -- it produces no escape, so no amount of classifying\nescape sites will ever surface it.\n\nI ALSO WROTE A TEST THAT BLESSES THE SHAPE. test_barren_seed_line_is_skipped\ndocuments \"a source line the DDG recorded nothing for contributes nothing\" as\nintended. That reasoning is right for a seed that is one of several and wrong\nas a licence for False.\n\nMINIMUM FIX (safe, and behaviour-neutral on output today because nothing acts\non False): a barren definition must yield None, not False. That makes False\nstrictly more conservative -- it can only prevent a false negative, never cause\none.\n\nREAL FIX, per the panel: refutation must be COVERAGE-GATED. Forfeit it for any\nfunction whose CFG statement extents do not cover every call node in the\nfunction body, which catches this class mechanically rather than by\nenumerating known gaps."  # d6f8
    fields:  # d6f8
      statement: "The section 3a walk may return False (everything accounted for) only when it actually followed the value at every step. A definition for which the DDG holds no entry at all must yield None."  # d6f8
      root_cause: "The walk continues past an empty use-set without setting escaped, so \"the extractor never recorded this definition\" is indistinguishable from \"this definition provably goes nowhere\". cfg_nodes/go.yaml self-documents a matching extraction gap (if/for initializers invisible to def/use), giving the defect a large real population."  # d6f8
- op: discuss  # 9708
  at: '2026-08-04T08:49:38Z'  # 9708
  by: agent  # 9708
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9708
  clock: 2  # 9708
  nonce: '9708'  # 9708
  message: "MINIMUM FIX SHIPPED in PR #199 (eedaad025d). STATUS STAYS violated -- see the\nresidual below. Behavioural evidence, the item's own filed repro re-run on\nmerged dev:\n\n  _ddg_taint_reaches(\"f\", [1], [9], {})  ->  None     (was False)\n\n  Production-reachable shape (a source with 2 call sites, one untracked):\n    seeds [3]   all tracked, closed cycle  ->  False   <- CONTROL: earned False\n    seeds [1,3] seed 1 untracked           ->  None    (was False)\n\n  Non-regression on the other outcomes:\n    escaped into a container -> None ; exhaustion -> False ; dependence -> True\n\nThe control matters: the fix does not blanket-return None, it degrades exactly\nthe unaccounted-for case.\n\nWHY THIS DOES NOT SATISFY THE INVARIANT. The statement says False may be\nreturned \"only when it actually followed the value at every step\". The fix\ncovers a TOTALLY barren definition -- the DDG holding no entry at all. A\nPARTIALLY recorded definition still returns False, and that is the shape the\ngo.yaml gap actually produces:\n\n    L1  v := source()\n    L2  w := f(v)                  <- recorded\n    L5  if n := sink(v); n > 0 {   <- use of v in an if-INITIALIZER, invisible\n\n  DDG holds {(f,1):{2}, (f,2):{1}} -- the line-5 use of v is absent. Every\n  frontier line has an entry, so nothing is barren and nothing escapes. The\n  walk returns False. Verified live on merged dev. True answer is True.\n\nSo the acute case is closed and the class is not. The remedy is the panel's\ncoverage gate, now filed separately (see the linked work item): forfeit\nrefutation for any function whose CFG statement extents fail to cover every\ncall node in its body. Closing this item on the minimum fix would be a\npartition dressed as a resolution (L14).\n\nCORRECTION TO THIS ITEM'S OWN EVIDENCE. The description states the panel\n\"reproduced the caddy incident flow through this path\" and traces it as \"the\nwalk pops line 4, finds no uses, continues, records NO escape, and returns\nFalse\". That does not reproduce. Measured by running the stated shape through\na reimplementation of the pre-fix walk beside the current one:\n\n    uses={(f,3):{4}} seeds=[3] sinks=[5]   OLD -> None    NEW -> None\n\nLine 4 is never popped. It fails the membership test one step earlier and hits\nthe ESCAPE branch, which already set escaped. The defect is real -- the bare\nrepro and the isolation pair both flip -- but that particular example was\nnever evidence for it, and a later reader should not inherit a trace that does\nnot reproduce. The barren branch is reachable ONLY for seed lines, because\nevery other frontier entry is membership-tested before being appended, and\npropagate_taint_ddg additionally gates on source_tracked = any(...), so a\nsource whose only call line is untracked never reaches the walk at all.\n\nALSO RETIRED: test_barren_seed_line_is_skipped, which documented the defect as\nintended behaviour. Its assertion passed for an unrelated reason (the None came\nfrom a later escape, not the barren seed), so it never exercised the branch it\nnamed -- a vacuous test guarding the exact line that was wrong."  # 9708
