  set:  # 5a25
    description: "VERIFIED LIVE DEFECT, ON CLAUSE L2. Re-run at dev 11a240f83d with the\npositive control passing:\n\n  defs_at={(f,1):{v}}, ddg_uses={(f,v,1):{2}},\n  callees_at={(f,2):{fmt.Printf}}, source_lines=[1], sink_lines=[5]\n\n    gate OFF                  ->  False   <- THE DEFECT\n    forfeit_refutation=True   ->  None    <- the coverage gate answers it\n    control (use at sink recorded) -> True\n    barren control (L1)       ->  None\n\nEvery frontier line HAS a DDG entry, so nothing is barren and nothing\nescapes -- and the walk still returns False, the only verdict that may ever\nlicense removing a reported flow, for a definition it did not follow at every\nstep. The true answer is True: v IS an argument at the sink call site.\n\nCLAUSE L1 IS CLOSED, and is recorded here rather than left at the head of\nthis item where it read as the live defect. As filed, L1 was\n_ddg_taint_reaches(\"f\", [1], [9], {}) -> False: a definition the DDG holds NO\nentry for, yielding the accounted-for verdict. PR #199 (eedaad025d) made that\nNone, and it still returns None at tip. Do not re-file it.\n\nMECHANISM (L1, for the record). The walk did `uses = ddg_uses.get((symbol_id,\nline))` and, when empty, `continue`d WITHOUT setting `escaped`. Every other\nway of losing the value sets it; that one did not. L2's mechanism is\ndifferent and is why the class is not closed: the use is not MISSING from the\nmap, it was never RECORDED by the extractor, so the walk sees a complete\npicture of an incomplete function.\n\nWHY IT IS NOT HYPOTHETICAL -- THE GAP IS SELF-DOCUMENTED. cfg_nodes/go.yaml\nsays, in the file itself:\n  \"Known gap, disclosed: the `initializer` of an if_statement\n   (`if err := do(); err != nil`) and of a for_clause is not reached by the\n   conditional/loop hooks... Those bindings are therefore still invisible to\n   def/use.\"\nThe panel counted 700 of 6,596 `if` statements in caddy carrying a call in the\ninitializer. So there is a large, known, per-language population of constructs\nthe def/use extractor does not see -- and the walk converts every one of them\ninto a confident negative instead of an unknown.\n\nTHE PANEL REPRODUCED THE CADDY INCIDENT FLOW THROUGH THIS PATH.\n  cwd, _ := os.Getwd()\n  msg := \"cwd=\" + cwd\n  if n, err := fmt.Printf(\"%s\", msg); ...\nyields exactly one DDG edge, (cwd, 3, 4). msg's use at line 5 does not exist in\nthe DDG. The walk pops line 4, finds no uses, continues, records NO escape, and\nreturns False. That is a REAL leak -- one of the three verified-real removals\nfrom the 2026-08-03 arm -- refuted with no escape flagged anywhere.\n\nRELATIONSHIP TO THE OTHER OPEN ITEMS. INV-busis frames the blocker as non-call\nescape sites needing field-sensitivity. This is a THIRD fact that framing\nmissed: not \"journey ended\", not \"went somewhere unfollowable\", but \"the use\nwas never recorded because the construct is not modelled\". Unlike the other\ntwo it is INVISIBLE -- it produces no escape, so no amount of classifying\nescape sites will ever surface it.\n\nI ALSO WROTE A TEST THAT BLESSES THE SHAPE. test_barren_seed_line_is_skipped\ndocuments \"a source line the DDG recorded nothing for contributes nothing\" as\nintended. That reasoning is right for a seed that is one of several and wrong\nas a licence for False.\n\nMINIMUM FIX -- SHIPPED, PR #199. A barren definition now yields None, not\nFalse. Closes L1 only. (The parenthetical it carried, \"behaviour-neutral on\noutput today because nothing acts on False\", has been FALSE since PR #214\ngave False a second consumer: the barrier arm earns `sanitized` on a False and\na sanitized flow is dropped from a claim's violation set.)\n\nREAL FIX, per the panel: refutation must be COVERAGE-GATED. Forfeit it for any\nfunction whose CFG statement extents do not cover every call node in the\nfunction body, which catches this class mechanically rather than by\nenumerating known gaps."  # 5a25
