- op: discuss  # f5cc
  at: '2026-08-17T22:55:42Z'  # f5cc
  by: agent  # f5cc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f5cc
  clock: 14  # f5cc
  nonce: f5cc  # f5cc
  message: "PRIORITY CHANGED 2026-08-17, on owner authorisation, as part of the P0/P1 sweep. Recording the reasoning here because a re-rank that lives only in conversation is indistinguishable next session from drift.\n\nTHE GATE. This item terminates at WI-kabif's removal authority, which is parked TWICE OVER: (1) a standing owner ruling of DO NOT START, and (2) a pre-registered numeric threshold -- measurement 0001 records that the removal-authority question becomes \"arguable on its merits\" near 80% precision, and states that no reading of the data supports a number near 80% (measured ~41%). So this is parked on a NUMBER, not on effort, and no amount of session time moves it.\n\nP0 -> P2. This was the tracker's ONLY P0 and sat at RANK 1 of 227 in tracker ready with no dependency edges, so every session picked it up first. Two facts make that ranking wrong:\n\n  1. IT CANNOT BE WORKED. The remaining clause is L2, and closing it means wiring the section 3a arm -- which this item's own thread, WI-joluk's description, and test_taint_refutation_gate_contract.py all say must land in the SAME PR as WI-kabif's removal authority. Wiring it alone is a measured no-op (the 3a arm tests `is True`, so False and None collapse).\n  2. IT CHANGES NOTHING TODAY. Across 85 production walks on two repos and two languages the walk returned False ZERO times.\n\nNOT A DOWNGRADE OF THE DEFECT. L2 re-reproduced at tip on 2026-08-17 with the positive control passing, and since PR #214 an unearned False DELETES a flow. The severity is unchanged; what changes is the claim that a session should work this before anything else. The tracker now has no P0, which is the honest reading: nothing is currently both critical and actionable."  # f5cc
- op: discuss  # dc2f
  at: '2026-08-25T04:13:58Z'  # dc2f
  by: agent  # dc2f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # dc2f
  clock: 15  # dc2f
  nonce: dc2f  # dc2f
  message: "PHASE 0 RE-VERIFICATION AT TIP, 2026-08-25, dev e41a655d6d. L2 STILL\nREPRODUCES AT THE UNIT LEVEL -- and is NOT a live fail-open on published\noutput. Both halves matter; the second is why this item leaves the campaign's\nPhase 1.\n\nTHE FILED REPRO, control printed first and admissible:\n    positive control (use at sink line recorded) -> True   ADMISSIBLE\n    L1 filed repro _ddg_taint_reaches(f,[1],[9],{}) -> None   (closed, PR #199)\n    L2 partially-recorded def, gate OFF          -> False  <- the defect\n    L2 same, forfeit_refutation=True             -> None\nIdentical to the 2026-08-17 sweep. Status stays violated.\n\nBUT False HAS EXACTLY TWO CONSUMERS AND NEITHER IS EXPOSED.\n  taint.py:3326 (section 3a arm) tests `is True`, so False and None collapse.\n  taint.py:3378 (barrier arm) DOES pass forfeit_refutation.\n\nAND THE COVERAGE PREDICATE FIRES ON THE MOTIVATING CONSTRUCT. Measured on a Go\nfixture carrying this item's own caddy shape, with a control in the same run:\n\n    ddg_symbols   : ['go:main.go:16-20:covered:function',\n                     'go:main.go:8-14:leak:function']\n    forfeit_refut : ['go:main.go:8-14:leak:function']   <- if-initializer, FORFEITED\n    edges         : leak    1  (cwd->msg only; msg's use never recorded)\n                    covered 2  (fully recorded)         <- CONTROL, not forfeited\n\nSo WI-joluk's gate catches exactly the class this item was filed for, and it\nis not vacuously forfeiting everything.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR THE CAMPAIGN. This item is correctly filed and correctly\nparked: closing L2 means wiring the section 3a arm, which this thread,\nWI-joluk and test_taint_refutation_gate_contract.py all say must land in the\nSAME PR as WI-kabif's removal authority -- and WI-kabif is parked on a NUMBER\n(measurement 0001 ~41% vs the ~80% at which removal authority becomes\narguable). Removed from the campaign's Phase 1 fail-open family; it is not\nproducing a false all-clear today. Not a downgrade of the defect."  # dc2f
- op: discuss  # cfce
  at: '2026-09-14T21:36:18Z'  # cfce
  by: agent  # cfce
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cfce
  clock: 16  # cfce
  nonce: cfce  # cfce
  message: "RE-VERIFIED AT TIP 2026-09-14, AND THE PARKING RATIONALE IS HALF STALE. Control\nprinted first, per the trap this thread records.\n\n    positive control (use at sink recorded)        -> True   ADMISSIBLE\n    L1 filed repro _ddg_taint_reaches(f,[1],[9],{}) -> None   CLOSED (PR #199)\n    L2 partially-recorded def, gate OFF            -> False  STILL REPRODUCES\n    L2 same, forfeit_refutation=True               -> None\n\nBOTH THINGS THIS ITEM WAS PARKED ON HAVE LANDED, and no entry on this thread\nsays so. WI-joluk is done and WI-kabif is done: 2fca492700 (2026-08-26) wired\nthe forfeit gate to the section 3a arm, and b26d97bd11 (2026-09-02) granted\nthat arm removal authority. The sequencing this thread demanded -- \"land the\n3a forfeit in the SAME PR as any 3a removal authority\" -- was honoured in the\nSAFE order, gate first, authority second, with the gate already in place.\nVerified in source, not from the commit subjects: both call sites now pass\nforfeit_refutation, and the 3a arm no longer collapses False with is-True.\n\nTHE 2026-08-17 P0->P2 REASONING HAD TWO LEGS AND ONE IS NOW FALSE.\n  \"IT CANNOT BE WORKED\" -- false. Both blockers are done; the work is\n      ordinary now.\n  \"IT CHANGES NOTHING TODAY\" -- still true, and re-measured below.\nPriority NOT changed here: that is the owner's call.\n\nA THIRD ROUTE TO AN UNEARNED False, FOUND AND CLOSED IN THIS PR. Not the\nfiled L1 or L2 shape and not WI-votom's two. In the heir loop, followed is a\nDISJUNCTION over heirs and an heir the DDG holds no uses for is skipped\nsilently -- so a RECORDED sibling closes the line on an UNRECORDED one's\nbehalf, via WI-votom's own permitting case (\"no call at this line at all, so\nthe heir really is the value's only exit\", which reasons about ONE heir).\nOne-variable isolation, controls either side:\n\n    CONTROL A (b recorded, reaches sink)        -> True   ADMISSIBLE\n    CONTROL B (sole heir b unrecorded)          -> None   <- already escaped\n    DROPPED HEIR (a recorded, b unrecorded)     -> False  <- THE DEFECT\n    DROPPED HEIR, forfeit_refutation=True       -> None\n\nCONTROL B is the argument: the walk ALREADY treats an heir with no recorded\nuses as unknown when it is alone. The multi-heir path simply disagreed with a\nruling the same function had shipped. WI-joluk's gate cannot reach this class\nat all -- it keys on CALL nodes and the motivating statement has none.\n\nTHIS ITEM DOES NOT CLOSE, AND HERE IS THE PROBE THAT SAYS SO. A second route\nsurvives the fix above: a missing USE rather than a missing heir, at a\nnon-call construct, where every heir IS tracked and every call IS covered, so\nneither the heir fix nor the coverage gate has a subject.\n\n    L1 cwd := src()        L2 a := cwd (recorded)     L3 print(a)\n    L4 for _, c := range cwd {   <- SECOND use of cwd, invisible (WI-losod)\n    L5     sink(c)               <- covered call\n\n    CONTROL (second use recorded)           -> True   ADMISSIBLE\n    RESIDUAL (second use unrecorded)        -> False  <- true answer True\n    RESIDUAL, forfeit_refutation=True       -> None\n\nThat is this item's clause L2 intact. It is the SECOND RESIDUAL the 2026-08-08\nentry recorded as \"read from cfg.py, NOT measured\"; it is now measured, and it\nis filed as WI-mugop-ravub-sobat-jotub-tulat-jikan-pogad-vufis rather than\nleft in this thread. That item carries the design question the fix must\nanswer FIRST: widening coverage past call nodes raises the forfeit share,\nand WI-joluk pre-registered 12.8-35.5% as what keeps refutation viable.\n\nBLAST RADIUS TODAY IS STILL ZERO, MEASURED, AND THE PRECONDITION IS NOT RARE.\nEvery production walk wrapped, tallied by arm and verdict, over real\nverify-claims runs:\n    hypergumbo-core, own claims, rc 3   84 walks   29 True / 55 None / 0 False\n    alertmanager, generic claims, rc 1  22 walks    8 True / 14 None / 0 False\nZero walks saved by the heir fix on either, because section 3a returns False\nZERO times on both -- escapes dominate, which is INV-busis from the other\nside. But the population the fix protects is large. Per inherits map:\n    hypergumbo-core  194177 entries   4281 multi-heir   1978 with an\n                     unrecorded heir  (up to 8 heirs on one statement)\n    alertmanager      12388 entries   2848 multi-heir    340 with an\n                     unrecorded heir\nThe class activates as escape sites close.\n\nINSTRUMENT CORRECTION, recorded because it nearly produced a false negative\nin the other direction: the first version of this harness reported ZERO\nmulti-heir sites. That was a silent no-op str.replace (the anchor was\nindented, the target was not), so the counter never printed. A zero beside an\nunexamined map is a blind instrument; the re-run prints the map size next to\nthe count so the two cannot be confused again."  # cfce
