  nonce: '2203'  # 2203
  message: "MERGED as PR #957 (dev 93d87de795). The heir-granularity route is closed; this\nitem STAYS VIOLATED on the route that survives it, which is filed as WI-mugop.\nPost-merge: dev level with origin, ratchet 669 delta +0, 4489 passed, 100%\ncoverage on changed files.\n\nNot closing, and stating the test rather than the verdict: this item closes\nwhen a partially-recorded definition can no longer yield False. It still can --\nthe probe on the previous entry shows a missing USE at a non-call construct\nreturning False with every heir tracked and every call covered. That is clause\nL2 intact."  # 2203
- op: discuss  # fefa
  at: '2026-09-14T23:57:30Z'  # fefa
  by: agent  # fefa
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fefa
  clock: 18  # fefa
  nonce: fefa  # fefa
  message: "WI-mugop SHIPPED AND CLOSED; THIS ITEM STAYS VIOLATED. Stating the test rather\nthan the verdict, because this item's own history is of people closing it on a\npartition.\n\nWHAT CHANGED. The coverage gate now asks about uncovered SEMANTIC LEAVES, not\nonly uncovered CALL nodes, so the route that survived PR #957 -- a missing USE\nat a non-call construct -- is gated in production. Verified through\nbuild_repo_ddg with a control: the range-clause function is walkable AND\nforfeited; the matched fully-recorded control is walkable and NOT forfeited.\nA/B on the same pair: leak [] -> [16], control [] -> [].\n\nWHY THIS DOES NOT DISCHARGE THE STATEMENT. The invariant is universal -- False\nonly when the walk followed the value at EVERY step. A coverage predicate\ncompares AST nodes against RECORDED CFG STATEMENT EXTENTS. At any predicate\nwidth it can establish \"a statement was recorded covering this region\"; it\ncannot establish \"every use inside that region was recorded\", because\npopulate_def_use_for_cfg runs the extractor ON the matched node and an omission\nINSIDE a covered extent leaves no uncovered region to find. Per this project's\nclosure-evidence discipline a proxy may supplement but never substitute, and\ncoverage is a proxy for completeness.\n\nAND I COULD NOT REPRODUCE THE RESIDUAL, which is worth more than the argument.\nThe obvious candidate was a use captured inside a Go func literal on a recorded\nline. It does not reproduce: the extractor records it correctly.\n\n    closureLeak: cwd def line 12 -> use line 13  AND  -> use line 15\n    walkable True, forfeited False -- and correctly so, nothing is missing.\n\nSo the residual clause is STRUCTURAL AND UNDEMONSTRATED. That is a materially\nweaker thing than L1 or L2 ever were, both of which had live repros on this\nthread from the day they were filed. Recorded as such rather than filed as a\nnew work item, because filing a speculative item would put an unreproduced\nconcern in the ready queue ahead of work that has evidence.\n\nWHAT A REPRO WOULD NEED: a construct the def/use extractor mis-handles while\nthe CFG still records a statement covering it, in a function that has other\nedges (so it is walkable), where the missed use reaches a sink. If one is\nfound, it is this item's clause L4 and the coverage approach is insufficient by\nconstruction rather than by width.\n\nSTATUS IS A QUESTION FOR THE OWNER, and I am deliberately not answering it.\nEvery route known to this thread is now gated and none currently reproduces,\nwhich is the definition of pending_validation (\"fix deployed but not yet\nvalidated\"). I am leaving it VIOLATED because this item was re-scoped rather\nthan closed twice before on exactly this kind of reasoning, and because\nINV-lupav's statement is the one the whole taint engine's negative results\nrest on. Moving it is your call."  # fefa
- op: discuss  # 4b15
  at: '2026-09-15T00:23:13Z'  # 4b15
  by: agent  # 4b15
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4b15
  clock: 19  # 4b15
  nonce: 4b15  # 4b15
  message: "CLAUSE L4 IS REPRODUCED. This corrects my own entry earlier today, which\nrecorded it as \"structural and UNDEMONSTRATED\" on the strength of one candidate\nshape that did not reproduce (a use captured in a Go func literal -- the\nextractor records that correctly). Guessing shapes was the wrong instrument.\nSweeping for them mechanically found three in twenty minutes.\n\nTHE SWEEP. For each recorded CfgStatement, match it back to its AST node by the\n(line, col, node_type) key the extractor itself uses, enumerate the identifier\nleaves inside it, and ask whether the statement's own defines/uses account for\neach name the function defines somewhere. A hit means: this function defines\nthis variable, this RECORDED statement mentions it, and the extractor recorded\nneither a def nor a use of it there. Instrument at\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/taint-area-08052026/meas/use_completeness_sweep.py,\ncontrol passing, candidates charged to the INNERMOST recorded statement.\n\nTHREE SHAPES READ BACK TO SOURCE:\n  go   grouped var declaration -- alertmanager api/v2/api.go:251 records\n       \"line 251 var_declaration defines=[] uses=[]\" for a block carrying three\n       definitions and a call argument.\n  go   defer -- both deferred_call and defer_statement record defines=[] uses=[]\n  py   subscript index -- \"counters[key] = 1\" records\n       \"defines=['counters'] uses=[]\"; the index is not a use.\n\nTHE UNEARNED False, through the production path, control first:\n    CONTROL (msg := cwd, recorded)     -> True    ADMISSIBLE\n    L4      (var block, unrecorded)    -> False   <- true answer True\n    l4leak walkable=True forfeited=FALSE   <- the gate is silent\n    edges l4leak  : cwd 13->14, a 14->15           (chain to sink GONE)\n    edges control : cwd 23->24, a 24->25, cwd 23->26, msg 26->27\nOne variable changed -- \"var ( msg = cwd )\" against \"msg := cwd\".\n\nWHAT THIS SETTLES ABOUT THIS ITEM. The coverage approach cannot close it. A\ncoverage predicate compares AST nodes to recorded statement EXTENTS, so it can\nestablish that a statement was recorded and never that its contents were\naccounted for; WI-mugop widened the predicate as far as the coverage NOTION\ngoes and this class sits underneath it. So the remedy is extractor-level, or a\ncompleteness signal that is not coverage-shaped -- the extractor reporting per\nstatement that it UNDERSTOOD the construct rather than merely matched it.\nFiled as WI-ninun-pipur-mokij-dagus-roliz-supas-logim-vunos.\n\nAND IT SETTLES THE STATUS QUESTION I LEFT OPEN EARLIER TODAY. I asked whether\nthis item should move to pending_validation on the grounds that every known\nroute was gated and none reproduced. That reasoning is now void: a route\nreproduces, it is live on the production path, and it deletes a flow. The item\nis VIOLATED on evidence again rather than on the absence of a counterexample,\nwhich is the better footing to be on. Do not move it.\n\nSECOND TRUST POINT, ENUMERATED HERE BECAUSE THIS THREAD HAS NEVER NAMED IT. The\nwalk reaches \"return False\" through exactly four paths that continue without\nsetting escaped: the seen-set cycle guard, followed-with-no-call-at-the-line,\nfollowed-with-a-terminating-callee, and no_heir-with-a-terminating-callee. TWO\nof the four rest on _use_site_terminates, i.e. on the summary CATALOGUE being\nright. A catalogue entry that wrongly declares a propagating function as\nconsume-and-discard produces an unearned False that no coverage gate can ever\nsee, because the walk did look and believed what it was told. That is a\nbounded, finite audit and it has never been done."  # 4b15
- op: discuss  # 4bfa
  at: '2026-09-15T02:35:47Z'  # 4bfa
  by: agent  # 4bfa
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4bfa
  clock: 20  # 4bfa
  nonce: 4bfa  # 4bfa
  message: "SATISFIED, ON THE FILED ROW, WITH THE ENUMERATION THAT MAKES IT CHECKABLE.\n\nTHE STATEMENT. \"The section 3a walk may return False (everything accounted for) only\nwhen it actually followed the value at every step. A definition for which the DDG holds\nno entry at all must yield None.\"\n\nWHY THIS CLOSES NOW AND NOT AFTER THE PREVIOUS THREE PRs. Every clause of this item was\nthe same defect wearing a different construct, and each was found by hunting for a shape.\nHunting does not terminate -- which is how this item reached six weeks. What terminates\nis the observation that _ddg_taint_reaches continues WITHOUT setting escaped in only\nfinitely many places, so they can be COUNTED. They are now counted, structurally, against\nthe AST of the shipped function:\n\n  1. the seen-set cycle guard                     -- already walking this pair\n  2. a barrier line                               -- a sanitizer consumed the value\n                                                     (barrier arm only; the arm with\n                                                      removal authority never sees it)\n  3. followed, and NO call at this line           -- pure rebinding\n  4. followed, and a catalogued consuming callee\n  5. no heir, and a catalogued consuming callee\n\ntest_walk_exit_census.py pins that count with three positive controls (add a sixth exit;\ndelete an escaped=True and watch an exit get reclassified; rename the walk and demand an\nerror rather than an empty census), plus a single-return-False assertion so every\naccounted path funnels through the one gate. A sixth exit is now a named test failure\ninstead of a six-week search that starts when somebody notices a deleted finding.\n\nTHE COUNT IN MY OWN NOTES SAID FOUR. It omitted the barrier exit. The census was off by\none before it was first executed, which is the argument for executing it rather than\nwriting it down.\n\nEACH EXIT, AUDITED, WITH THE PR THAT CLOSED IT.\n  1  correct by construction.\n  2  correct by construction; and it cannot fire on the removal-authority arm.\n  3  needs `followed` to be COMPLETE over heirs. #957: a recorded sibling was closing\n     the line on an unrecorded one's behalf.\n  4, 5  rest entirely on the CATALOGUE. #961: fmt.Fprintf and fmt.Fprintln carried the\n     positive dead-end marker while writing into argument 0. Terminating set now a\n     37-entry census with controls.\n\nAND THE WALK'S INPUT IS NOW GUARDED BY TWO COMPLEMENTARY SIGNALS, which is the other\nhalf of the statement:\n  EXTENT coverage  (#959, WI-joluk widened by WI-mugop) -- code OUTSIDE every recorded\n                   statement. Forfeits per FUNCTION.\n  CONTENT coverage (this PR, clause L4) -- a variable mentioned INSIDE a recorded\n                   statement that accounts for it nowhere. Escapes per VARIABLE.\nNeither is a per-language list of constructs; both ask a structural question through the\nsame _is_semantic_leaf predicate, so neither decays as grammars change. That property is\nthe reason this closes as an invariant rather than as a pile of fixed shapes.\n\nCLOSURE EVIDENCE -- FIFTEEN CASES, CONTROLS FIRST, ZERO UNCLOSED.\n  5 controls (one per language, plus Go's UNGROUPED var, one token from the defect):\n      nothing flagged by either signal.\n  7 L4 shapes (go grouped var x2; py subscript / aug-subscript / slice index / del c[t];\n      ts template substitution): caught by unaccounted_names.\n  3 shapes leaving an uncovered region (py with open(t), ts for..of, rust for..in):\n      caught by the coverage gate, which fails SAFE on them.\n\nLIVE REPRO ON THE PRODUCTION PATH, control printed first, one variable apart, both\nfunctions walkable and both reporting full coverage:\n    covered   gate=silent  unaccounted={}     -> True    ADMISSIBLE\n    leak      gate=silent  unaccounted={cwd}  -> False   <- the defect\n    leak      with the signal                 -> None    unaccounted_mention@12\n\nTHE FILED L1 AND L2 REPROS, RE-RUN.\n  L1  _ddg_taint_reaches(f,[1],[9],{}) -> None. Still closed (PR #199).\n  L2  the partially-recorded definition: in PRODUCTION the missing use now comes with\n      evidence -- the caddy shape (if err := do(); err != nil) leaves an uncovered\n      region and the coverage gate fires. At the raw INDEX level, handed a hand-built\n      incomplete map and no evidence of incompleteness, the walk still returns False and\n      MUST: it cannot know what it was not told. The invariant is about what production\n      hands it, and production no longer hands it an incomplete picture silently.\n\nMEASURED EFFECT ON VERDICTS TODAY IS ZERO AND IS REPORTED AS ZERO. Paired arms, the real\nwalk called twice on identical inputs:\n    hypergumbo-core own claims    84 walks   34 handed a signal   2 raised   0 moved\n    ~/repos/alertmanager generic  22 walks    8 handed a signal   1 raised   0 moved\nZero because section 3a returns False ZERO times on either repo (55/13 escaped, 29/9\nconfirmed) -- INV-busis from the other side. The guard is live semantics over a class\nthat is currently empty, and it activates as escape sites close.\n\nRESIDUAL, FILED NOT BURIED (WI-buzup): the L4 signal is TEXTUAL, so an unaccounted use at\na statement that does not NAME the variable -- alias-shaped -- is outside it by\nconstruction. Two probes do not reproduce (a read through the alias chains correctly and\nreturns True; a write through it escapes source_undefined), so it is a disclosed limit\nawaiting a sweep, not a defect. Do not re-open this item on it without a reproduced case.\n\nSECOND RESIDUAL, ALREADY OWNED: exits 4 and 5 rest on catalogue DATA, guarded by a census\nsnapshot rather than a structural check. \"Does this callee really consume and discard?\" is\nnot machine-checkable; \"did the set change?\" is, and that is what the census asserts.\nINV-dohoj and WI-potan carry the follow-on."  # 4bfa
